# Chat (live server, UI-08 / B-32; named only: ui_* stays out of the /REPLAY default set): the saved channels' rejoin
# at world entry and the Set Channels window's join and leave. Zanor (avatar 6, docked) has Channel_Newbie on (player100663360_options.ini), so the chat panel's first
# update in the world (ui_chat_panel.cpp 0x5630B0 -> ChatPanelInterface::Unknown_56B700 0x56B700) sends a
# CLIENT_CHAT_REQUEST type 6 for 'New Players', one per option-enabled channel whose number is "5" (0xB7C530), then
# type 0x1D (RestrictedStatus off). Set Channels (UIOptionChannelClass, opt06a) with General Chat ticked and OK sends
# type 6 'General' itself (0x5C93B0 -> 0x5C9580); Quit to Character Selection and Enter make a new chat panel whose
# rejoin sends 'New Players' and 'General'; General unticked and OK sends type 7 (0x5C9740) and leaves the options as
# they were.
# The request's payload (Net-7 PacketStructures.h ClientChatRequest): PlayerID, type (4 bytes each), three strings
# (2-byte length, text), a 4-byte data size. The client puts the channel in the second string and " " in the third,
# the first empty (B-32: ours put the name first and " " second until 2026-11-27). The bytes are logged only by a
# diagnostic antprox-rs (T1, 2026-11-27: ANTPROX_DUMP_OPCODES=00a3 appends ', N bytes: HEX' to the verbose 'Sending
# [0x00a3] via UDP'); with the stock proxy the hex steps below cannot match, so run it with that build (ANTPROX_EXE):
# a clone of AntaresProxy-Rust at the store's antprox-rs commit (baselines/tools/antprox/manifest.json, 9601958),
# tools/harness/antprox_dump_patch.py on its crates/antprox/src/net7/udp_link.rs, cargo build --release (40 s).
# Run: ANTPROX_DUMP_OPCODES=00a3 ANTPROX_EXE=<that build> e2e.py --live --instance NAME [--retail] run ui_chat_rejoin
name: chat channels (live): the saved channels' rejoin at world entry, Set Channels join / leave, the rejoin after Quit to Character Selection, a /gen line
timeout: 400
include _login_live
# the login's rejoin: type 6, '' / 'New Players' / ' ', data size 0 (30 bytes)
expect-event antprox 'via UDP, 30 bytes: [0-9a-f]{8}0600000000000b004e657720506c617965727301002000000000 ' within 20
expect-event antprox 'via UDP, 18 bytes: [0-9a-f]{8}1d000000' within 20
# Set Channels: General Chat ticked, OK: type 6 'General' from the window itself (26 bytes)
click gadget chat.tab.chat
alive 0.5
click gadget chat.channels
expect-event proxy 'opt06a\.ini", R, disposition 3\) = ok' within 10
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 15
click 572,347
alive 0.5
shot channels_general_ticked
click 471,596
expect-event antprox 'via UDP, 26 bytes: [0-9a-f]{8}060000000000070047656e6572616c01002000000000 ' within 10
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 15
# Quit to Character Selection and back in: a new chat panel, its rejoin
key esc
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 15
click gadget quit.charselect
wait-event antprox 'GLOBAL_AVATAR_LIST' within 60
wait-quiet proxy 1.5 within 40
click gadget select.slot0
click gadget select.enter until antprox 'received LOGIN' redo 1 every 1 within 60
wait-event antprox 'received START_ACK' within 120
wait-quiet proxy 1.5 within 60
expect-event antprox 'via UDP, 30 bytes: [0-9a-f]{8}0600000000000b004e657720506c617965727301002000000000 ' within 20
expect-event antprox 'via UDP, 26 bytes: [0-9a-f]{8}060000000000070047656e6572616c01002000000000 ' within 20
# B-21: '/gen hi' typed (SClient 0x749ED0): the channel in the second string, the first empty, the text third; the
# server, the channel joined, sends the line back as a CLIENT_CHAT_EVENT
key enter
alive 0.5
text '/gen hi'
key enter
expect-event antprox 'via UDP, \d+ bytes: [0-9a-f]{16}0000070047656e6572616c02006869' within 10
expect-event antprox 'sent CLIENT_CHAT_EVENT' within 10
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 15
# General unticked, OK: type 7 'General', no third string (25 bytes); the options as they were
click gadget chat.tab.chat
alive 0.5
click gadget chat.channels
expect-event proxy 'opt06a\.ini", R, disposition 3\) = ok' within 10
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 15
click 572,347
alive 0.5
click 471,596
expect-event antprox 'via UDP, 25 bytes: [0-9a-f]{8}070000000000070047656e6572616c000000000000 ' within 10
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 15
